SWEET gesture sysctl (patch 0312, ALL-ON T-31, coordinator 2026-11-11: the nav must check the UI state before every step): kern.sweetgesture (write, root, struct sweet_gesture {magic 'SGST', id, x0, y0, x1, y1, ms}) injects ONE tap (x0==x1, y0==y1, held ms) or drag (finger moves every 10 ms over ms (the nav session tick; 8 ms steps did not trigger the bottom-edge home swipe, T-36)) on the HID work loop; refused EBUSY while a nav session / script / gesture runs, EINVAL outside 1080x2400 or ms not 20..2000. Lines 'SWEET GESTURE: id N begin ... now NS' / 'end now NS' (kernel clock of the SWEET NAV markers). kern.sweetfbcount (read) = swaps + distinct frames presented (2 x u64) for a 'UI settled' test. A userland driver (pixnav) reads the screen (kern.sweetpanel, patch 0276), classifies it, and decides the next gesture: navigation by intent with a state check, never a timed blind tap. Replaces the kernel-side recovery of the withdrawn patch 0311. Input injection + counter reads only: no register, no store to hardware.
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp
@@ -398,6 +398,12 @@
